// ha.proto — DashCenter northbound HA control & telemetry API.
//
// This service exposes the upstream DASH HA model (10-state DPU machine,
// 5-state flow-sync, perfect-sync colour-flip) at the operator surface.
// Read RPCs reflect the current role/state of each HA scope and set;
// mutating RPCs trigger operator-initiated switchover or failover with
// per-phase progress streamed back.
//
// Relationship to upstream
// ------------------------
// The 10-state DPU role machine and 5-state flow-sync state are defined in
// sonic-net/DASH (specs/dash-ha-scope-orchestration, dash-ha-set-fsm). We
// mirror their semantics here but expose them as a clean operator-facing
// enum: HaScopeRole has 12 entries (10 upstream + UNSPECIFIED +
// TRANSITIONING), FlowSyncState has 5 entries (NONE, INITIATING, SYNCING,
// SYNCED, FAILED).
//
// Switchover vs failover
// ----------------------
// Switchover = planned, coordinated role flip. The current active first
// drains, then the standby promotes. Used during maintenance.
//
// Failover = unplanned, fast role flip. Trigger when the operator has
// independently confirmed the active DPU is dead and does not want to wait
// for dashd's health-check budget to expire. There is NO drain.

